<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42303" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sălax</span></b> , ācis,
			adj.
		salio; cf. sagax, from sagio. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Fond of leaping</i>, esp. of male animals, <i>lustful</i>, <i>lecherous</i>, <i>salacious</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">galli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 9, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aries,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 771</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salaciora animalia, Lact. Opif. Dei, 14:
					salacissimi mares,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					7, 9, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">8, 2, 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cauda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 2, 45</span></i>
			.—Vulgarly applied to Priapus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Priap. 14, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">34, 1</span></i>; and sarcastically: salacissimus
			Juppiter, Sen. ap. <i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 16,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b> transf., <i>that provokes
				lust</i>, <i>provocative</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">erucae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am. 799</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bulbi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					3, 75, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">herba, i.e. eruca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 2, 422</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 48, 10</span></i>.</div>
